    "lawCode": "Amd §1174, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9504A\n\nSPONSOR: COONEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to increasing\npenalties for violation of overtaking and passing a school bus\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo increase the penalties for passing a stopped school bus.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends Subdivision c of section 1174 of the vehicle and traf-\nfic law to allow for additional penalties for an individual convicted of\npassing a stopped school bus. It increases the maximum fine for a third\nor subsequent conviction within three years from $1000 to $1500.\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nDespite the current penalties available for passing a stopped school bus\nand the creation of camera programs, motorists continue to disregard\nschool bus \"STOP\" arms and lights. Recently, in the village of Fayette-\nville, NY a motorist was caught passing a stopped on the right side,\nnearly striking a 5-year old. Increasing the maximum fine for someone\nthat commits multiple offenses will provide an additional deterrent.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-22: Referred to Transportation\n\n2019-2020: Referred to Transportation\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first of November next succeeding the\ndate on which it shall have become a law and shall apply to violations\noccurring on and after such date. Effective immediately, the addition,\namendment and/or repeal of any rule or regulation necessary for the\nimplementatiOn of this act on its effective date are authorized to be\nmade and completed on or before such effective date.\n",
